// specs.memql
//
// Deployment-namespace specs. The Deployment Console
// (znasllc-io/memql#725 + #728) is gated to owner/admin; this context-
// spec mirrors the canonical requiresAdmin in dsl/_reference/_spec.memql
// and binds to the actorEnvelope @actor shape so it evaluates
// in-process against the auth context. The DeployControlService Go
// layer enforces the same predicate via auth.AtLeastAdmin; this spec
// is the DSL-side mirror so policies / queries can delegate to it via
// spec("requiresOwnerOrAdmin").
//
// #1872 (persisted deployments) reuses this same owner/admin gate for
// the deployment-lifecycle mutations: mutationCreateDeployment +
// mutationUpdateDeploymentStatus (dsl/cluster/mutations.memql) are only
// ever invoked from the owner/admin-gated DeployControlService write
// RPCs, so the deploy-start write and every status transition inherit
// the same authorization decision the console read/write path enforces.
//
// #1877 (cut a version) reuses the SAME gate: the SuggestNextVersion
// (read) + CutVersion (write) RPCs both run s.authorize -> owner/admin,
// and CutVersion creates the new pending deployment via that same
// mutationCreateDeployment -- so the cut-version path inherits this
// predicate too. owner/admin gating is sufficient for now; the
// developer-role split is tracked separately in #1876.

use common.shapes.{ actorEnvelope }

@enabled
@description("Caller must hold owner or admin role to use the Deployment Console.")
@shape("actorEnvelope")
spec requiresOwnerOrAdmin {
  actor.role == "admin" || actor.role == "owner"
}
